# Root-level ignore for `vercel deploy` invoked from the repo root, needed
# because Project Settings -> Root Directory ("backend") is applied on top of
# whatever the CLI uploads, and a bare `cd backend && vercel deploy` double-
# applies that path. Deploying from the repo root instead requires this file,
# or the upload includes mobile/ and node_modules/ (over 1GB).
mobile/
node_modules/
backend/node_modules/
backend/.venv/
backend/__pycache__/
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.ruff_cache/
backend/tests/
backend/fixtures/
.git/
docs/
web/

# CRITICAL: Vercel prefers pyproject.toml over requirements.txt when present,
# and backend/pyproject.toml declares NO runtime dependencies (it is only
# ruff/pytest/pyright config). Shipping it makes the build install nothing and
# every request fail with FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED. backend/.vercelignore
# excludes it for the same reason; this file must too.
backend/pyproject.toml
